# Steering docs are deliberately kept out of this public repo -- they carry candid
# internal reasoning (VAC-risk research, safety-flag interruptions, killstreak/MP
# motivations) not meant for a public GitHub audience. Both files live one directory
# up from this repo root as of the 2026-08-05 move and are never meant to be copied
# back in, but ignored here too as a defensive safety net, same pattern as this
# file's other "never meant to land in the repo" entries below.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Build outputs (proxy DLL is deployed straight into the game root, not committed)
proxy_d3d9/obj/
proxy_d3d9/Debug/
proxy_d3d9/Release/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.log
*.exp
*.lib
d3d9.dll

# Never commit a copy of any Microsoft system DLL, even accidentally staged for testing.
d3d9_orig.dll

# User-generated config (task #14) -- written fresh with defaults by mod_config.cpp
# on first run at the game root, never meant to be committed (personal tuning values).
mw3ncp_config.ini

# User's own scratch live-test notes (jotted during playtests, read back in during
# dev sessions) -- personal working notes, not a project doc, never meant to be committed.
notes.txt

# Build OUTPUTS ONLY for dev-only tools under tools/ -- these tools are not shipped
# with the mod itself, but their SOURCE is real, tracked, committed code (ui_harness
# in particular is a genuine standalone app with real ongoing development value, not
# a disposable script -- only its compiled .exe/.dll/.obj are excluded here, same
# "source tracked, build output ignored" policy this repo already applies to
# proxy_d3d9 itself). Double-star so this also covers nested sub-projects (e.g.
# tools/ui_harness/ui_hot/bin/), not just one level deep.
tools/**/bin/
tools/**/obj/
vcontroller_sim.exe
memdiff.exe
regbreak.exe

# memdiff full-process memory snapshots (~400MB each) -- diagnostic scratch data, never
# meant to be committed
tools/memdiff/*.snap

# xenia_probe (2026-08-03, Xenia/Xbox 360 console ground-truth research) -- its guest-RAM
# snapshots (~512MB each) and paired screenshots are diagnostic scratch data, same policy
# as memdiff's own .snap files above and the dumps/ policy below. Only the tool's own
# source (main.cpp) and throwaway analysis scripts are committed.
tools/xenia_probe/*.snap
tools/xenia_probe/*.bmp
tools/xenia_probe/*.png
tools/xenia_probe/xenia_probe.exe

# Third-party reference material (cloned locally for research only -- learn from and
# independently re-verify, never blindly reuse; see re_notes for how any lead from here
# gets treated). Not ours to redistribute as part of this repo.
references/

# Extracted MW3 game assets (from OpenAssetTools' Unlinker, run against our own retail
# .ff fastfiles for RE purposes -- see re_notes/iw5sp.md) are Activision's copyrighted
# game data, never ours to redistribute. Dumped outside this repo by default (D:\Tools),
# but ignored here too as a defensive safety net in case any dump output ever lands
# inside the repo by accident.
zone_dump/
ff_dump/
*.gdt

# Full-process MiniDumpWriteDump snapshots + matching screenshots (2026-08-02, issue #51
# live-memory-analysis toolchain) -- ~1-2GB each, kept locally on purpose for ongoing
# offline analysis (menu-position calibration, future killstreak/other investigation
# passes per project notes), never meant to be committed.
dumps/

# ui_harness diagram anchor editor output (2026-08-05, issue #66) -- a scratch
# hand-off file (drag positions in the harness, read the numbers back out here),
# never a source of truth on its own; the real defaults live in overlay_hud.cpp's
# own kDiagLayout* constexpr tables once copied over.
tools/ui_harness/exported_diagram_layout.txt

# Ghidra project for iw5sp.exe (2026-08-25, issue #90) -- a real, regenerable
# (~124s headless import+analysis) binary database, not source. Kept on disk
# across sessions so RE work doesn't re-pay the analysis time, but never
# committed -- too large (166MB+) and not meaningful to diff/review.
re_notes/ghidra_project/
